---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy of Plans65: no ZIP code, no phone, no agent leads" description="What Plans65 processes: no cookie, no account, no ZIP code, phone number or health details collected, nothing passed to insurers or agents. Your rights under the GDPR and US state laws." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. People comparing Medicare coverage are among the most solicited consumers in the country: a ZIP code and a phone number left on a plan site often bring calls for weeks. This site asks for neither. Its publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to what the site does, for every visitor; residents of US states with a consumer privacy law keep at least the rights below.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>Your state, county, income, drug costs, date of birth or plan choices are computed in your browser. When you pick another state, the browser downloads that state's public plan file from this site; the request contains only the file name, such as "fl.json", never what you typed. "Copy share link" writes your inputs into the page address: whoever receives the link can read them.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>GitHub, the host, records the IP address, time, page and browser of each request for security. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention: GitHub's policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Cookie-free stability monitoring</h3><p>Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited) is loaded in a mode that sets no cookie and does not link visits; it measures errors, load times and clicks that do nothing, with page content and all typed values masked. Microsoft receives the technical request data, including the IP address. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a working site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object by blocking clarity.ms or by writing to us.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics</h3><p>No analytics, advertising or social media script is loaded today. Before any stability tool is switched on, this page will name it and say how to refuse it.</p></>}
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write, we keep your address and message to answer, and delete them three years after the last exchange. Please do not send your Medicare number, Social Security number or health information: we never need them.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no leads</h2><p>We sell and share no personal information, pass nothing to insurers, agents, brokers or marketing organizations, and build no profiles.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers</h2><p>GitHub, Inc. is in the United States; request data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability and objection: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, answer within one month. You may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is meant for adults choosing health coverage and collects nothing from children.</p>
    <p>See the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
